{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And you shall be to Me a treasure (segulah).</b> The hidden and concealed treasure, kept from the eye, is called סגולה — a thing set apart and beloved to the king, under his hand; over it he will not appoint an officer nor assign a sheriff or ruler, in the manner of what is written (Ecclesiastes 2:8): ״וסגולת מלכים והמדינות.״ And for this reason He said, ״from all the peoples״ — that is, this distinction does not belong to the other peoples, for they are under the governance of the king's officers and sheriffs. And Scripture explicitly states (Deuteronomy 4:19): ״אשר חלק ה׳ אלהיך אותם לכל העמים״ — ״which HaShem your Elohim has allotted to all the peoples״ — and of Israel He said ״ואתכם לקח ה׳״ — ״but you HaShem has taken״ — for Israel are taken as His allotted portion, blessed be He, and are a סגולה under His hand in uniqueness." "<b>For all the earth is Mine.</b> And I did not choose any nation or tongue but you. <br><b>By way of the Kabbalah:</b> ״For all the earth is Mine״ — I have already alluded to the matter of the earth called כל in the verse of Genesis."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:01.062388127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}